{"availability":"available","full":"MasakiNiwa/InBrowser-JustText","name":"InBrowser-JustText","description":"Edit text files in your browser and save them — find & replace, encoding detection, offline, 15 languages.","category":"Developer tools","language":"JavaScript","stars":0,"forks":0,"created":"2026-08-28T03:39:37Z","updated":"2026-10-11T09:59:28Z","license":"MIT","branch":"main","homepage":"https://masakiniwa.github.io/InBrowser-JustText/","topics":["android","encoding","offline-first","pwa","text-editor"],"demo":"https://masakiniwa.github.io/InBrowser-JustText/","color":"#193546","ink":"#a6d6e8","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-17T21:13:28.953Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-17T21:13:28.953Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-17T21:13:28.953Z","metrics":[{"at":"2026-10-11T19:51:00.515Z","stars":0,"forks":0},{"at":"2026-10-17T21:13:28.953Z","stars":0,"forks":0}],"technologies":[],"overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["Edit text in your browser and save it. Nothing more.","It exists because Android has no built-in way to edit a JSON or config file, and installing an app just for that is a lot to ask. Your files never leave the device — reading and saving both happen inside the browser.","When reading, the BOM, escape sequences, byte validity and how much the result looks like real text are checked in that order. If the guess is wrong, tap UTF-8 ▾ at the bottom of the screen to reopen with another encoding (LF ▾ next to it is the line ending used when saving)."],"features":["Choose location — pick a folder and file name. Picking an existing file overwrites it","Overwrite — appears once a location has been chosen; writes straight back to the same file"],"sourceUrl":"https://github.com/MasakiNiwa/InBrowser-JustText/blob/main/README.md","fingerprint":"cf9aae59acb4d24992b9e83d3a7629bda1339a0bc42cc625d8f1502c747260fb","extractedAt":"2026-10-11T19:51:00.643Z"},"overviewCheckedAt":"2026-10-11T19:51:00.643Z","projectInsights":{"version":1,"whatItDoes":{"text":"Edit text in